{"id": "EUVD-2026-107248", "enisaUuid": "62e2bf4f-ea18-3da4-92e2-cd304f31bbe8", "description": "Trudesk through 1.2.11 contains a regular expression injection vulnerability that allows unauthenticated attackers to enumerate usernames by submitting regex patterns to POST /api/v1/login. Attackers can send alternations or prefixes like (admin|root) or a.* and distinguish 'Invalid User' from 'Invalid Password' responses to discover valid accounts.", "datePublished": "2026-10-21T12:39:54", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T19:57:13", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@leediay/multiple-vuln-trudesk-1211", "https://github.com/polonel/trudesk/blob/v1.2.11/src/models/user.js#L310-L319", "https://github.com/polonel/trudesk/blob/v1.2.11/src/controllers/api/v1/common.js#L45-L65", "https://github.com/polonel/trudesk", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/trudesk-through-1.2.11-username-enumeration-via-regex-injection-in-api-v1-login"], "aliases": ["GHSA-m446-w75v-4fjm", "CVE-2026-114401"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.44, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "f323f202-16ba-32df-8f00-4a5f795f9429", "product": {"name": "trudesk", "vendor": {"name": "polonel"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22641.2.11"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "651776cc-3260-33ba-a806-d13df51d3ad0", "vendor": {"name": "polonel"}}], "isExploited": false}